   "status": "model",
   "name": "The Oak Leaf — massing",
   "note": "The house proposed for the knoll, at real size: four leaf lobes round the river-stone chimney that stands here today — kitchen and master reaching north, lounge and suites south — the great room under the tall one, a loft over it, three suites cut into the south bank with the parking court below, the pool and the fire terrace on the north side, the drive out to the street. The model's origin is the chimney; its main floor is the top of the knoll at 425.9 m. The outline is the BUILT ground only — the oak lounge and the sacred garden's stepping stones are deliberately left outside it, because the recorded oaks standing there are the point of those two places and the map must not clear them. A massing, not a design: the shape at the right size on the right ground, to be walked round and argued with. Made by scripts/oak-leaf.py in the pack repository and published with it — the world loads the built file rather than building one at deploy. Rebuilt 2026-09-20 from 51,348 triangles to 4,830, uncompressed: the same building generated sparse rather than decimated, verified by an identical bounding box and an identical set of floor and solid names.",
